cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Value-Field Theory (VFT)"
message: "If you use this theory or repository, please cite this repository."
authors:
  - family-names: "Nuno"
    given-names: "T."
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher"
abstract: >
  Value-Field Theory (VFT) is a structural framework for describing how
  real resource and capital states K and nominal or expectation structures P
  jointly generate directional attraction for actions and resource or liquidity
  flows. The framework separates expectation stock P from expected flow
  E[Delta K], treats preference and rationality differences as differences in
  the structure and magnitude of P, and treats observed economic and social
  data as proxies used to operationalize the theoretical variables K, P, A,
  and Delta K.
repository-code: "https://github.com/nuno929/vf-model"
license: "CC-BY-4.0"
keywords:
  - value-field theory
  - resource dynamics
  - expectation field
  - expectation stock
  - nominal-real structure
  - resource flow
  - measurement proxy
  - social dynamics
